<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria M1 rises 4.88 pct, M2 up 2.62 pct in week.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria M1 rises 4.88 pct, M2 up 2.62 pct in week.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgarian M1 money supply rose to 1.176 trillion levs on July 18 from 1.121 trillion levs a week earlier and M2 increased to 4.383 trillion levs from 4.271 trillion levs, preliminary central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>Total broad money rose 2.66 percent to 4.611 trillion levs in the week to July 18.</p>
<p>Conversion of foreign currency-denominated deposits into levs was made at the central bank fixing of 1,000 levs per mark for July 11 and July 18 and 990.6 for June 27.</p>
<p>The lev was pegged at 1,000 per mark on July 1 under an IMF-prescribed fixed exchange rate mechanism, known as a currency board system.</p>
<p>The system requires levs in circulation to be fully matched by central bank foreign exchange reserves.</p>
